    <bpmn:process id="W_W1026" name="W1026. Vendor Product Discontinuation Notification &amp; Last-Time Buy Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Vendor notifies BuildRight of product discontinuation; or Category Manager identifies vendor intent to discontinue during quarterly business review
Frequency: ~30–50 discontinuation events/month (~360–600/year) across the 35,000 active SKU base
Volume: 1 SKU or SKU range per event; average 3–8 SKUs per discontinuation event
Owner: Category Manager
Participants: Vendor, Buyer, Merchandise Planner, Supply Chain Planner, Store Operations Coordinator, Marketing Coordinator
Source: workflow W1026 — Vendor Product Discontinuation Notification &amp; Last-Time Buy Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1026_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1026_Lane1" name="Buyer">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1026_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1026_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1026_Lane2" name="Category Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1026_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1026_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1026_Lane3" name="Merchandise Planner">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1026_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1026_Lane4" name="Store Operations Coordinator">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1026_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1026_End12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1026_Start6" name="Vendor notifies BuildRight of product discontinuation; or Category Manager identifies…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1026_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1026_Task7" name="Discontinuation Notification Receipt &amp; Validation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Discontinuation Notification Receipt &amp; Validation: Vendor notifies BuildRight of product discontinuation via: (a) vendor portal (W868) — vendor uploads discontinuation notice with effective date and last-order date; (b) email/letter from vendor sales representative; (c) discovery during vendor QBR (W706) or JBP session (W155); (d) Buyer enters discontinuation notice into system: SKU(s) affected, vendor-stated reason, vendor last-order date (deadline for BuildRight to place final order), vendor last-ship date (final delivery date), and warranty/support commitment period for already-sold units; (e) system validates: (i) are there open POs for affected SKUs? (ii) current on-hand inventory at stores and DCs? (iii) is the SKU part of any active promotional plan, bundle (W910), or project price book (W163)? (iv) are there active B2B blanket purchase agreements (W979) referencing the SKU?
Responsible (R): Buyer
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 15–30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1026_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1026_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1026_Task8" name="Impact Assessment &amp; Replacement Analysis">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Impact Assessment &amp; Replacement Analysis: Category Manager and Buyer assess impact: (a) Sales impact: system retrieves trailing 12-month sales velocity by store cluster, channel (in-store, ecommerce, B2B), and customer segment; calculate annualized revenue and margin impact; (b) Customer impact: identify trade accounts with recurring purchase history for the SKU; flag for proactive outreach; (c) Replacement product: (i) does vendor offer a direct successor model? if yes, evaluate specifications, pricing, and compatibility with existing customer applications; (ii) if no successor, can alternative vendor supply equivalent product? evaluate per W631 (Strategic Sourcing); (iii) if no equivalent exists, assess whether BuildRight should source private label replacement per W129; (d) Inventory disposition plan: (i) current on-hand + in-transit + on-order quantities vs. expected sell-through rate; (ii) if current inventory exceeds expected sell-through before discontinuation date: reduce/cancel open POs; (iii) if current inventory is insufficient: calculate last-time buy quantity
Responsible (R): Category Manager / Buyer
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 1–3 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1026_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1026_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1026_Task9" name="Last-Time Buy (LTB) Quantity Calculation &amp; Order">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Last-Time Buy (LTB) Quantity Calculation &amp; Order: Merchandise Planner calculates LTB: (a) LTB quantity = (average monthly demand × months of coverage needed) − current on-hand − in-transit − confirmed open PO quantities; (b) months of coverage = min(12 months, remaining product lifecycle per replacement timeline); (c) adjust for seasonal demand patterns — cement demand peaks in dry season (Mar–Apr), paint peaks in Jan–Feb; (d) LTB must be placed before vendor&#x27;s last-order date; (e) Buyer places LTB PO with vendor per W2; (f) for imported items with 45–90 day lead times, LTB must account for extended lead time; (g) system marks affected SKU(s) as &quot;discontinued — sell-through&quot; status: (i) no new replenishment orders will be generated by auto-replenishment (W2A); (ii) existing inventory available for sale until depleted; (iii) SKU removed from active assortment plan per W679 (Assortment Optimization)
Responsible (R): Merchandise Planner / Buyer
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 30–60 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1026_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1026_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1026_Task10" name="Stakeholder Communication &amp; Transition Execution">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Stakeholder Communication &amp; Transition Execution: (a) Store Operations: Store Operations Coordinator distributes discontinuation notice to all stores: SKU details, expected sell-through period, replacement product (if any), clearance timeline; stores begin positioning discontinued items for clearance per W93 (Markdown &amp; Clearance Pricing); (b) Ecommerce: Marketing Coordinator updates buildright.com.ph: remove product listing once inventory is depleted; if replacement product exists, set up URL redirect from old product page to new product page for SEO preservation per W563; update product comparison tool per W940; (c) B2B/Trade Accounts: Account Manager proactively contacts trade accounts with purchase history for the SKU: notify of discontinuation, offer LTB opportunity, introduce replacement product with sample or demo per W1007; update project price books (W163) and blanket purchase agreements (W979) with replacement SKU; (d) Loyalty/CRM: update customer wishlist alerts per W934 if discontinued SKU was on wishlists; (e) Service &amp; Warranty: update service center (W440) on parts and service availability for discontinued power tools per vendor warranty commitment period
Responsible (R): Store Operations Coordinator / Marketing Coordinator / Account Manager
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 2–4 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1026_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1026_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1026_Task11" name="Sell-Through Monitoring &amp; Final Clearance">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Sell-Through Monitoring &amp; Final Clearance: Monthly monitoring: (a) system tracks sell-through rate of discontinued inventory vs. plan; (b) if sell-through is slower than expected: (i) progressive markdown schedule: 15% at month 3, 25% at month 4, 40% at month 5, 50%+ at month 6; (ii) bundle with complementary products per W910 to accelerate movement; (iii) offer to wholesale channel per W598 at bulk discount; (c) if any inventory remains after 6 months of sell-through period: system generates write-off request per W220 (SLOB Provisioning) with approval by Category Manager and Finance Controller; (d) upon final unit sold or written off: system updates SKU lifecycle status to &quot;inactive,&quot; removes from store replenishment parameters (W312), and archives product data per W316 (Digital Asset Master)
Responsible (R): Category Manager / Merchandise Planner
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 30 min/month per event</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1026_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1026_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1026_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1026_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1026_Annotation13">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-247 (ensure controlled execution — Purchase Order Cycle (PA-03.2).) | - operational: vendor buy-back or trade-in program for orphaned accessories per W916
Owner: Category Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1026_Assoc14" sourceRef="W1026_Annotation13" targetRef="W1026_Start6" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1026_Flow15" sourceRef="W1026_Start6" targetRef="W1026_Task7" />
