    <bpmn:process id="W_W1137" name="W1137. Vendor Purchase Order Line-Level Partial Shipment Acceptance &amp; Backorder Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Vendor delivers partial shipment against a multi-line purchase order, or vendor notifies of partial shipment capability
Frequency: ~360–480 partial shipments/month (~30–40% of the ~1,200 merchandise POs)
Volume: 2–5 PO lines affected per partial shipment
Owner: Buyer
Participants: Buyer, DC Receiving Team, Vendor, Supply Chain Planner
Source: workflow W1137 — Vendor Purchase Order Line-Level Partial Shipment Acceptance &amp; Backorder Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1137_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1137_Lane1" name="Buyer">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1137_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1137_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1137_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1137_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1137_Lane2" name="DC Receiving Team">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1137_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1137_Lane3" name="AP Team">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1137_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1137_End11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1137_Start5" name="Vendor delivers partial shipment against a multi-line purchase order, or vendor notifies…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1137_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1137_Task6" name="Partial Shipment Notification &amp; Pre-Receipt Planning">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Partial Shipment Notification &amp; Pre-Receipt Planning: (a) vendor notifies Buyer of partial shipment via vendor portal (W866) or email: which lines are shipping now, which lines are backordered, expected ship date for backordered lines; (b) system updates PO: shipped lines marked &quot;In Transit,&quot; backordered lines marked &quot;Backorder&quot; with expected date; (c) if backorder will cause stockout at store level: Buyer evaluates options — source from alternate vendor (W631), transfer from another DC (W218), or adjust store replenishment allocation (W105); (d) DC receiving team notified of incoming partial shipment for dock scheduling (W585)
Responsible (R): Buyer / System
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 10–15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1137_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1137_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1137_Task7" name="Partial Goods Receipt Processing">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Partial Goods Receipt Processing: (a) DC Receiving Team processes delivery against PO: scan each received line, confirm quantity received vs. quantity ordered; (b) for fully received lines: system marks line as &quot;Received Complete&quot;; (c) for partially received lines: system records quantity received and marks remaining as backordered; (d) for lines not received at all: system confirms backorder status; (e) receiving team flags any quality issues (damaged packaging, wrong items) per W681 (DC quality control); (f) system updates inventory for received quantities only; (g) goods receipt document generated showing received vs. backordered quantities
Responsible (R): DC Receiving Team / System
Accountable (A): DC Operations Manager
Duration: 10–20 min per PO</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1137_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1137_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1137_Task8" name="Backorder Tracking &amp; Vendor Follow-Up">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Backorder Tracking &amp; Vendor Follow-Up: (a) system generates backorder aging report: PO number, line item, quantity backordered, original promised date, revised expected date, days overdue; (b) Buyer reviews backorder report daily and follows up with vendors: confirm expected delivery date, escalate if overdue &gt; 7 days, negotiate partial delivery of backordered quantity if possible; (c) for critical items (A-class SKUs representing 80% of revenue): Buyer escalates to VP Merchandising for vendor intervention; (d) system tracks backorder fulfillment rate per vendor — feeds into vendor performance scorecard (W706)
Responsible (R): Buyer
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 30–60 min/day</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1137_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1137_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1137_Task9" name="Partial Invoice Processing &amp; 3-Way Match">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Partial Invoice Processing &amp; 3-Way Match: (a) vendor submits invoice for partial shipment via vendor portal (W867); (b) AP team performs 3-way match (W7): PO line quantity ordered vs. GR quantity received vs. invoice quantity; (c) for partial shipments: system matches invoice only against received quantities; (d) backordered quantities not invoiced until delivered; (e) if vendor invoices for backordered quantities before delivery: AP rejects invoice line and notifies Buyer; (f) freight cost allocated proportionally across received quantities (not backordered quantities)
Responsible (R): AP Team / System
Accountable (A): Finance Manager
Duration: 5–10 min per invoice</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1137_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1137_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1137_Task10" name="Backorder Resolution &amp; PO Closure">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Backorder Resolution &amp; PO Closure: (a) when vendor ships backordered lines: goods receipt processed per Step 2; (b) if backorder extends beyond useful timeframe (seasonal item past season, or customer demand has shifted): Buyer cancels backorder with vendor, PO line closed; (c) if vendor cannot fulfill backorder: Buyer sources alternate supply per W631 or W670; (d) PO closed when all lines are either received complete, cancelled, or closed by Buyer; (e) final PO fulfillment rate calculated: total quantity received ÷ total quantity ordered, tracked per vendor for sourcing decisions
Responsible (R): Buyer / System
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 10–15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1137_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1137_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1137_End11" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1137_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1137_Annotation12">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-247 (ensure controlled execution — Purchase Order Cycle (PA-03.2).) | - operational: Buyer review and approval gate
Owner: Buyer</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1137_Assoc13" sourceRef="W1137_Annotation12" targetRef="W1137_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1137_Flow14" sourceRef="W1137_Start5" targetRef="W1137_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1137_Flow15" sourceRef="W1137_Task6" targetRef="W1137_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1137_Flow16" sourceRef="W1137_Task7" targetRef="W1137_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1137_Flow17" sourceRef="W1137_Task8" targetRef="W1137_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1137_Flow18" sourceRef="W1137_Task9" targetRef="W1137_Task10" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1137_Flow19" sourceRef="W1137_Task10" targetRef="W1137_End11" />
    </bpmn:process>
    <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="W1137_diag">
      <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="W1137_plane" bpmnElement="W_W1137">
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1137_Lane1_di" bpmnElement="W1137_Lane1" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="80" width="1370" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
