    <bpmn:process id="W_W5567" name="W5567. Procurement-Impersonation &amp; Fake-PO Goods-Diversion Response" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: A supplier reports receiving BuildRight purchase orders nobody placed — fake PO documents, spoofed buyer email or chat instructions, or release/pickup directions to a carrier BuildRight never booked — or order-to-receipt reconciliation (W1006/W2) shows goods delivered to an address or collected by a party BuildRight never designated
Frequency: Rare but a recognized B2B fraud class: ~1–2 confirmed attempts per year across the ~800–1,000-vendor base, spiking after any public data exposure of buyer names, PO formats or delivery-site details
Volume: 1 event × the affected supplier&#x27;s shipments (typically 1–5 truckloads of diverted goods per attempt) × the supplier-notification and verification wave across the exposed category&#x27;s vendor list
Owner: Procurement Specialist (event owner); VP Legal &amp; Compliance (impersonation &amp; no-liability posture)
Participants: Buyer (category owner), Supplier (victim of the impersonation), AP/Finance (no genuine payable exists — the W770/W556 rails stay silent), VS-100 (fraudulent-document &amp; demand response), IT Security (spoofed-domain/mailbox forensics per W383/W5518), Loss Prevention (W839 case where an insider fed the fraud), VS-27.3 (look-alike domain takedown), VS-63 (store receiving alert on diverted POs)
Source: workflow W5567 — Procurement-Impersonation &amp; Fake-PO Goods-Diversion Response</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W5567_LaneSet7">
        <bpmn:lane id="W5567_Lane1" name="Procurement Specialist">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5567_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5567_Start8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5567_Lane2" name="IT Security">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5567_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5567_Lane3" name="Procurement">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5567_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5567_Task15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5567_Lane4" name="VS-63">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5567_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5567_Lane5" name="VP Legal">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5567_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5567_Lane6" name="Loss Prevention">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5567_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5567_End16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W5567_Start8" name="A supplier reports receiving BuildRight purchase orders nobody placed — fake PO…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5567_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5567_Task9" name="Verify &amp; void">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Verify &amp; void: confirm the reported PO carries a number/format BuildRight never issued (W2&#x27;s numbering, buyer codes, site conventions); issue the supplier a written void-order notice on authenticated channels — fraudulent orders are void ab initio and create no BuildRight obligation
Responsible (R): Procurement Specialist / VP Legal
Accountable (A): VP Legal &amp; Compliance
Duration: Same day</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5567_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5567_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5567_Task10" name="Preserve &amp; trace">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Preserve &amp; trace: secure the fake documents, headers and pickup instructions; IT Security pulls mail-log evidence of spoofing or a compromised buyer mailbox (W383/W5518); trace the pickup carrier and delivery address with the supplier for recovery and the police report
Responsible (R): IT Security / Procurement
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: 1–3 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5567_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5567_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5567_Task11" name="Supplier wave">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Supplier wave: notify the exposed category&#x27;s vendor list through the vendor portal (W62-class channels) — BuildRight POs are validated through the portal only; never act on email-, chat- or phone-originated order or release changes; single verification contact published
Responsible (R): Procurement / VS-03 portal admin
Accountable (A): Procurement Manager
Duration: 3–5 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5567_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5567_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5567_Task12" name="Receiving alert">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Receiving alert: stores and DCs flagged to hold any inbound shipment matching the diverted POs (number, SKU set, carrier); matched loads documented and the supplier&#x27;s genuine re-delivery prioritized
Responsible (R): VS-63 / Store &amp; DC Receiving
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: Same window</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5567_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5567_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5567_Task13" name="Law-enforcement &amp; infrastructure action">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Law-enforcement &amp; infrastructure action: evidence pack to the PNP Anti-Cybercrime Group; look-alike domain and spoofed-mail infrastructure takedown via VS-27.3; fraudulent-document response under VS-100
Responsible (R): VP Legal / VS-27.3
Accountable (A): VP Legal &amp; Compliance
Duration: 1–2 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5567_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5567_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5567_Task14" name="Insider check">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Insider check: where the fraud used genuine PO formats or unannounced site details, LP reviews access and conduct per W839 before the event closes
Responsible (R): Loss Prevention / Internal Audit
Accountable (A): VP Legal &amp; Compliance
Duration: Per case</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5567_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5567_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5567_Task15" name="PO-integrity retrofit">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: PO-integrity retrofit: portal-side PO authentication (digital order codes suppliers can self-verify), buyer-contact change protocol with dual-channel callback, and the supplier-verification clause added to W62-class contracts
Responsible (R): Procurement / IT
Accountable (A): CPO
Duration: 2–6 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5567_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5567_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W5567_End16" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W5567_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W5567_Annotation17">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-247 (ensure controlled execution — Purchase Order Cycle (PA-03.2).) | - operational: suppliers are notified that orders validate through the portal only, with reported fake POs voided in writing within 24 hours; diverted PO numbers are hold-flagged at receiving until the event closes; any suspected insider dimension is referred to LP/W839 before closure
Owner: Procurement Specialist (event owner); VP Legal &amp; Compliance (impersonation &amp; no-liability posture)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W5567_Assoc18" sourceRef="W5567_Annotation17" targetRef="W5567_Start8" associationDirection="None" />
